# --- Two PCs / ngrok setup: point frontend at the backend API ---
# Set this when the frontend runs on a different machine (e.g. ngrok) than the backend.
# Use the backend's ngrok URL so login and all data (files, stats) use the same API.
#
# Example: backend runs on PC A and is exposed as https://abc123.ngrok-free.app
#          frontend runs on PC B → create frontend/.env with:
# VITE_API_URL=https://abc123.ngrok-free.app
#
# Optional: when using the dev-server proxy (no VITE_API_URL), proxy target is taken from:
# VITE_PROXY_TARGET=https://your-backend-ngrok-url.ngrok-free.app
# (Falls back to VITE_API_URL, then http://localhost:8000)

# VITE_API_URL=
# VITE_PROXY_TARGET=
